.\" Manpage for muffinctl
.TH MUFFINCTL 1 "2026-05-28" "1.0" "muffinctl man page"

.SH NAME
muffinctl \- wmctrl-like window and workspace control for Cinnamon on X11 and Wayland

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B muffinctl
<command> [options]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmuffinctl\fP is a command-line utility for controlling windows and workspaces in the Cinnamon desktop environment. It provides wmctrl-like functionality and works on both X11 and Wayland sessions by communicating with the muffin-window-control Cinnamon extension via D-Bus.

.SH REQUIREMENTS
The "Muffin Window Control" Cinnamon extension must be enabled. Enable it via:
.br
\fBcinnamon-extensions -e muffin-window-control@mehran\fP
.br
or through Cinnamon Settings > Extensions.
.PP
Project: https://github.com/Mehran-user/muffinctl

.SH COMMANDS

.SS "Window Control"
.TP
.BI "list " [-a, --all]
List windows on the current workspace. Use \fB-a\fP or \fB--all\fP to list windows across all workspaces.
.TP
.BI "activate " <winId>
Activate and focus the specified window.
.TP
.BI "close " <winId>
Close the specified window.
.TP
.BI "minimize " <winId>
Minimize the specified window.
.TP
.BI "maximize " <winId>
Maximize the specified window.
.TP
.BI "unmaximize " <winId>
Restore a maximized window to its normal size.
.TP
.BI "fullscreen " <winId>
Make the specified window fullscreen.
.TP
.BI "unfullscreen " <winId>
Exit fullscreen mode for the specified window.
.TP
.BI "shade " <winId>
Shade (roll up) the specified window to its title bar.
.TP
.BI "unshade " <winId>
Unshade a rolled-up window.
.TP
.BI "toggleshade " <winId>
Toggle the shade state of the specified window.
.TP
.BI "raise " <winId>
Raise the specified window above others.
.TP
.BI "lower " <winId>
Lower the specified window below others.
.TP
.BI "move " <winId> <x> <y>
Move the specified window to coordinates (\fIx\fP, \fIy\fP).
.TP
.BI "resize " <winId> <width> <height>
Resize the specified window to \fIwidth\fP x \fIheight\fP.
.TP
.BI "moveresize " <winId> <x> <y> <width> <height>
Move and resize the specified window in a single operation.
.TP
.BI "sticky " <winId> [on|off]
Make the window appear on all workspaces. Defaults to \fBon\fP if no argument is given.
.TP
.BI "alwaysontop " <winId> [on|off]
Set or unset the window to always stay on top. Defaults to \fBon\fP.
.TP
.BI "skippager " <winId> [on|off]
Hide the window from the workspace pager. Defaults to \fBon\fP.
.TP
.BI "skiptaskbar " <winId> [on|off]
Hide the window from the taskbar. Defaults to \fBon\fP.

.SS "Window Search"
.TP
.BI "search " <pattern>
Search for windows by title, WM_CLASS, or WM_CLASS instance. Case-insensitive.
.TP
.B active
Display the currently active (focused) window's ID and title.

.SS "Workspace Control"
.TP
.B ws-list
List all workspaces with their names and active status.
.TP
.BI "ws-switch " <index>
Switch to the workspace at the given 0-based \fIindex\fP.
.TP
.B ws-add
Add a new workspace at the end of the list.
.TP
.BI "ws-remove " <index>
Remove the workspace at the given \fIindex\fP.
.TP
.BI "ws-rename " <index> <name>
Rename the workspace at the given \fIindex\fP.

.SS "Workspace Assignment"
.TP
.BI "ws-move " <winId> <wsIndex>
Move the specified window to the workspace at \fIwsIndex\fP.

.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
Window and workspace lists are displayed in tab-separated columns. The output format adapts based on available tools (\fBjq\fP, \fBpython3\fP, or plain text fallback).

Window list columns: \fBwinId\fP, \fBworkspace\fP, \fBtitle\fP
.br
Workspace list columns: \fBWorkspace index\fP, \fBname\fP, \fBactive status\fP

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List all windows across all workspaces:
.B muffinctl list -a
.TP
Find Firefox windows:
.B muffinctl search firefox
.TP
Activate a window by ID:
.B muffinctl activate 123
.TP
Move and resize a window:
.B muffinctl moveresize 123 100 100 800 600
.TP
List workspaces:
.B muffinctl ws-list
.TP
Switch to workspace 1:
.B muffinctl ws-switch 1
.TP
Move window 123 to workspace 2:
.B muffinctl ws-move 123 2

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
D-Bus session bus address. Used to communicate with the Cinnamon extension.

.SH NOTES
Window IDs are stable sequence numbers assigned by Muffin/Cinnamon. They may change across sessions.

.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/Mehran-user/muffinctl

